course: dictionary
lesson: 12450
title: Formal words in rules and news
level: primary-6
stars: 1
explain: «Deem» is a formal word. It means to think or judge something in a certain way, often by an official person or group. Everyday words like think, consider and judge are close in meaning, but deem sounds more serious and official.
explain: You will often meet «deemed» in rules, news and exam papers. «The water was deemed safe» means that someone checked the water and judged it to be safe. The clue is in the sentence: the water was checked, and the result was a decision.
explain: Try the swap test. Put «judged to be» or «considered» in place of deem. If the sentence still makes sense, you have found its meaning. «The bridge was deemed unsafe» becomes «The bridge was judged to be unsafe», which fits perfectly.
fact: Deem means to consider or judge something in a particular way.
fact: The forms are deem, deems, deemed and deeming.
fact: «Deemed» often means that someone official has made a decision, as in «if deemed necessary».
fact: «Deem» is a formal word, so it is common in rules, news and exams, but not in chatty talk.
fact: Synonyms for deem include consider, judge and regard, but deem sounds more official.
exercise: «The bridge was deemed unsafe, so it was closed.» What does deemed mean here? | Painted | Rebuilt | Lost | *Judged to be
exercise: Mia says deem means dream. What does deem actually mean? | To buy something cheap | To break into small pieces | To sleep and dream | *To consider or judge something a certain way
exercise: «The water was deemed safe.» Which word could replace deemed without changing the meaning? | shaken | hidden | *considered | forgotten
test: «Any answer deemed incorrect will not score a mark.» What does deemed incorrect mean? | *Judged to be wrong | Copied from a friend | Written in red ink | Checked twice
test: «The school deemed the trip too risky.» What does this tell us? | The school loved the trip | The school forgot about the trip | *The school judged the trip to be too risky | The trip was cancelled by rain
exam: «If deemed necessary, the teacher will call home.» What does deemed necessary mean? | Written down twice | *Judged to be needed | Forgotten by everyone | Shouted loudly
